  "id": "first-rank-symptoms",
  "term": "first-rank symptoms",
  "definition": "First-rank symptoms are experiences described by Kurt Schneider as occurring in many people with schizophrenia, in which thoughts, actions, or perceptions feel controlled or produced by an outside force rather than by oneself. Examples mentioned in the source include thought insertion, thought broadcasting or withdrawal, delusional perception, and \"made\" impulses or voluntary acts.",
